abstract: >-
  Independent replication and extension of a disaster-aware geographic
  healthcare accessibility methodology (Macharia et al., Kenya, 2025
  preprint), applied to the January 2021 South Kalimantan, Indonesia
  floods. Extends the methodology with district-level healthcare
  workforce capacity stratification and event-specific flood disruption
  modeling from Sentinel-1 SAR-observed extent, compared directly
  against a static hazard-risk proxy under matched conditions.
